% Test cases for the cold therapy policy (cold_therapy.le): synthetic claims
% for the two codes the LCD and Policy Article name. The policy concludes
% nothing — LCD L33735 denies the cold pad with pump as not reasonable and
% necessary and states no criterion for anything else — so every claim fails
% at the question, however complete its documentation, and no change of the
% record makes one payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base cold_therapy cases includes these resources:
    cold_therapy.

the knowledge base cold_therapy cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A fully documented claim for a cold pad with pump (E0218): the standard
% written order, the delivery and its proof, a home — denied as not
% reasonable and necessary all the same, and nothing flips it.
scenario cold_pad_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the cold pad.
    the HCPCS code of the cold pad is "E0218".
    the cold pad is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the order for the cold pad is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the cold pad is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the cold pad includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the cold pad includes order date.
    the order for the cold pad includes description of the item.
    the order for the cold pad includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the cold pad includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the cold pad was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the cold pad was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the cold pad.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].
    flip expects changes [].

% A reusable cold wrap (A9273): in scope, in the benefit, no criterion
% covers it.
scenario cold_wrap is:
    claim 1 is for the cold wrap.
    the HCPCS code of the cold wrap is "A9273".
    the cold wrap is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A cold pad furnished to a hospital inpatient: the hospital is not a home,
% so the claim fails already at applicability.
scenario cold_pad_in_hospital is:
    claim 1 is for the cold pad.
    the HCPCS code of the cold pad is "E0218".
    the cold pad is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is hospital.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A code no policy of the model decides (a chemical cold pack, A9270, is
% the seat lift policy's code; E1399 is nobody's): out of scope.
scenario miscellaneous_code is:
    claim 1 is for the cold device.
    the HCPCS code of the cold device is "E1399".
    the cold device is furnished to Dee.
    the residence of Dee is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
